"Weathered Wooden Porch"
"Protected by a thatch-covered roof, the old porch has survived the ravages of

weather and countless years well, although not without evidence of their

passage.  Underfoot, the planks of the floor are gray with age and dust, a few

of the boards cracked or even broken.  Even the ceiling shows signs of wear,

where a patch of mildewed thatch hides in a corner.  The porch leads into the

structure to the south, through a open doorway or westward, down a shallow

series of steps to the path.

