#39108
"Before a Roaring Fire"
"Quiet and comfortable, the room is heated by the blaze of a pine wood fire,

burning in a great gaping fireplace, centered on the back wall.  A pair of

over-stuffed chairs flank the stone-crafted hearth, taking advantage of the

warmth.  The walls of the room are draped with aging tapestries, holding at

bay the chill emanating from the stone.  The wall hangings are frayed and

faded, the colors dimmed by wood smoke and time.  Tables sit to one side of

each chair, each holding a candleholder and a half-burned taper.  The two

common rooms lie to the south and east, but the noise of the patrons chatter

is muffled in the peaceful room.

"
""
