#39112
"Common Room - Wayfarer's Inn"
"A single lantern suspended from a chain anchored to the ceiling, lights the

common room, doing little to dispel shadows that stretch out into dark corners

and offer an anonymity of sorts to those seated there.  The room, itself, is a

strange mixture of new construction and scavenged materials; the timbers

forming the rafters are new, the bar scarred by fallen debris.  The furniture

is hand-made, roughly crafted from green wood.  Behind the bar, nailed to the

wall and hanging at a drunken angle is an unframed painting, its fine detail

clearly marking it as a masterpiece.

"
